non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, copy and modify the Software for
personal noncommercial purposes, including personal English learning and
private study. Personal interview preparation or learning work-related
English does not, by itself, make an individual's independent study commercial.
Anyone may inspect the publicly available source to understand the project.

Individuals may redistribute the Software and modifications only without
charge and for personal noncommercial purposes. Such copies must retain this
license, copyright and third-party notices, identify modifications, and offer
no broader rights to project-owned material covered by this license. No right
to sublicense that material under different terms is granted.

2. Commercial authorization
Commercial use requires a separate written license from yomage-ai before
that use begins. Commercial use includes selling or licensing the Software;
using it to provide paid, advertising-supported or revenue-generating
services; integrating it into commercial products; and deploying or using it
on behalf of a business for internal operations, employee training or client
work. Noncommercial use of an organization's product or service is not
personal use under section 1 merely because its end users pay nothing.

Request commercial authorization through the repository's Issues contact:
https://github.com/yomage-ai/english-speaking-coach/issues
Submitting a request, receiving no reply, downloading a release, or making
a donation does not itself grant commercial authorization. Only an express
written agreement from the copyright holder does so.

3. Prior MIT rights remain
Versions v0.2.9 and earlier were released under the MIT License reproduced
below. This license does not revoke, replace or restrict permissions already
granted for that material, including when it remains in a later release.
New original material released under this license is subject to sections 1
and 2. Merely changing the release number or this license does not turn
previously MIT-licensed code into exclusively noncommercial code. Recipients
may continue to exercise MIT rights for the material covered by MIT.

4. Third-party material, learning data and names
Third-party components remain under their own licenses. Their notices are
included with release programs in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt or *.NOTICES.txt;
this license imposes no additional restrictions on those components.
This license does not claim ownership of a learner's data or impose these
Software-use restrictions on their own practice records or learning output.
It grants no trademark or endorsement rights. Access to Codex, model services
and operating-system features remains subject to their respective terms.

